.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt PLAKAR-RSYNC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm plakar-rsync
.Nd rsync daemon integration for plakar
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
integration package provides a source connector that backs up a module
served by an rsync daemon, or a directory or a single file inside it,
and a destination connector that restores into a directory of a module.
.Pp
Each backup lists the module in a single connection.
File content is fetched, one connection per file,
only for files whose metadata differs from the previous snapshot.
.Pp
Each restored file and symlink is sent on its own connection.
Directories get their final permissions and times at the end.
Existing files are overwritten and other files are left in place.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The source and the destination take the same configuration parameters:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar location
The location in the form
.Li rsync://[<user>[:<password>]@]<host>[:<port>][/<module>[/<path>]] .
.It Ar module
The module, if not given in
.Ar location .
.It Ar root
A directory appended to the path given in
.Ar location .
A destination directory is created if missing.
.It Ar port
The daemon port, if not given in
.Ar location ,
873 by default.
.It Ar username
The module user, if not given in
.Ar location .
.It Ar password
The module password, if not given in
.Ar location .
.It Ar max_connections
The maximum number of concurrent connections to the daemon, 4 by default.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Configure a source for the
.Li pub
module of an rsync daemon:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ plakar source add myrsync rsync://bob@rsync.example.org/pub password=secret
.Ed
.Pp
Supposing that a Kloset store named
.Li mystore
is already configured,
back up the module to this store:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ plakar at @mystore backup @myrsync
.Ed
.Pp
Restore a snapshot into the
.Li restore
module:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ plakar destination add myrsyncdst \
    rsync://bob@rsync.example.org/restore password=secret
$ plakar at @mystore restore -to @myrsyncdst <snapid>
.Ed
.Sh CAVEATS
Only the rsync daemon protocol is supported, not rsync over a remote shell.
.Pp
The client speaks protocol 27: modification times have a one second
resolution, and hard links are stored as separate files.
.Pp
Devices, named pipes and sockets are reported as errors and not backed up,
nor restored.
Extended attributes are neither backed up nor restored.
.Pp
A destination module needs
.Li read only = no ,
and
.Li use chroot = yes
to restore symlink targets as they are.
Owners and groups are restored only by a daemon running as root, or with
.Li fake super = yes .
.Pp
A changed file is fetched in full.
Each fetched file costs one connection and handshake.
.Pp
The snapshot is not atomic: a file changed between the listing and its
fetch is stored as fetched.
